    <briefdescription>
<para>Collects timed text and writes it out as a SubRip (.srt) subtitle file. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The writer holds a single open cue and closes it only when the text changes, so a caller can feed it every update without filtering out repetitions. Changes arriving faster than minimumCueDuration() are folded into the open cue instead of producing subtitles too short to read.</para>
<para>The caller owns the clock: it passes the elapsed time of every cue and the final duration to <ref refid="classQfSubtitleWriter_1a6b2a455c319b0101b3c5288d68fc79f8" kindref="member">write()</ref>, which keeps the cue timeline expressed against the media itself. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
